WEBVTT

00:00:06.308 --> 00:00:09.540
Blog Love by Chris Moore.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.731
Published by Mary Glasgow magazines.

00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:15.012
A division of scholastic limited.

00:00:15.072 --> 00:00:20.754
Chapter 1 Right to Me.

00:00:20.814 --> 00:00:28.028
Monday, July the 11th, 1539.

00:00:28.088 --> 00:00:33.325
I'm writing this blog in the Double Becca Internet Cafe in London.

00:00:33.385 --> 00:00:39.431
The cafe is in a tall, old, red London bus next to my language school.

00:00:39.491 --> 00:00:40.611
I love it.

00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:42.602
It's very British.

00:00:42.662 --> 00:00:47.793
I'm from Tokyo, but I'm living in the UK for three months.

00:00:47.853 --> 00:00:50.433
I'm learning English here.

00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:52.424
My name's Junko.

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:54.024
This is me.

00:00:54.084 --> 00:00:59.922
I've got black hair, dark eyes, glasses, and a big smile.

00:00:59.982 --> 00:01:02.620
Please write me at my blog.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.561
Goodbye for today.

00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:07.732
Zero messages.

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:13.716
First day July the 14th, 1542.

00:01:13.776 --> 00:01:21.870
Internet, I'm telling you about my life in England because you are my only friend here.

00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:25.622
I'm living with Mr. and Mrs. Lacey.

00:01:25.682 --> 00:01:28.519
Mr. Lacey works in a cinema.

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:31.756
Mrs. Lacy is a police woman.

00:01:31.816 --> 00:01:34.849
They always ask me the same thing.

00:01:34.909 --> 00:01:36.800
How are you today?

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.302
Okay, I answer.

00:01:39.362 --> 00:01:45.006
I ask about London, but Mr. Lacy says, let's talk this evening.

00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:46.887
I'm going to work now.

00:01:46.947 --> 00:01:48.498
Goodbye, Junco.

00:01:48.558 --> 00:01:50.576
Have a good day.

00:01:50.636 --> 00:01:58.148
In the evenings, I say hello to Mr. Lacey, but he says, I'm very, very tired.

00:01:58.208 --> 00:02:00.410
A terrible day at the cinema.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.170
I'm going to bed now.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.752
Good night.

00:02:03.812 --> 00:02:07.394
Sometimes I feel very lonely.

00:02:07.454 --> 00:02:10.606
Zero messages.

00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:15.749
Tuesday, July 19th, 1556.

00:02:15.809 --> 00:02:17.890
Hello, Internet.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.082
You are not my only friend in England.

00:02:21.142 --> 00:02:27.483
In the street next to the internet cafe, a girl says to me, you're Japanese.

00:02:27.543 --> 00:02:30.064
I know your face from language school.

00:02:30.124 --> 00:02:31.644
I'm Sonia.

00:02:31.704 --> 00:02:33.595
I'm from Slovakia.

00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:35.275
What's your name?

00:02:35.335 --> 00:02:37.026
I'm Junko.

00:02:37.086 --> 00:02:38.856
Junko Nagai.

00:02:38.916 --> 00:02:43.617
Sonia has dark hair and green eyes and expensive jeans.

00:02:43.677 --> 00:02:46.068
I love Japan, she says.

00:02:46.128 --> 00:02:47.488
Do you know Japan?

00:02:47.548 --> 00:02:48.684
I ask.

00:02:48.744 --> 00:02:51.162
I know Japanese mobile phones.

00:02:51.222 --> 00:02:52.954
They are my favorite.

00:02:53.014 --> 00:02:55.566
We look at my mobile.

00:02:55.626 --> 00:02:57.428
That's cool.

00:02:57.488 --> 00:02:59.120
I want one too.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.912
Have you got a boyfriend in England?

00:03:01.972 --> 00:03:03.103
No.

00:03:03.162 --> 00:03:05.796
Which boys do you like in school?

00:03:05.855 --> 00:03:07.567
I like Sylvia.

00:03:07.627 --> 00:03:10.600
He's closer from Sergio Tachini.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.073
I like English boys too.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:17.676
They drive cool cars and they've got great mobile phones.

00:03:17.736 --> 00:03:19.496
Have you got a car?

00:03:19.556 --> 00:03:24.588
My father's buying me a Passat, but I want Mercedes.

00:03:24.648 --> 00:03:27.900
Zero messages.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.826
Thursday, July the 21st, 1515.

00:03:32.886 --> 00:03:37.603
50 of us from school are in Oxford.

00:03:37.663 --> 00:03:40.646
It's an hour from London on the train.

00:03:40.706 --> 00:03:44.838
Oxford is famous because lots of students live here.

00:03:44.898 --> 00:03:47.230
Sonia is very happy.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.052
Oxford students have loads of money, she says.

00:03:51.112 --> 00:03:53.534
But I'm not happy.

00:03:53.594 --> 00:03:56.016
Sonia isn't talking to me today.

00:03:56.076 --> 00:03:58.628
She is always with Sylvia.

00:03:58.688 --> 00:04:00.935
Sylvia is from Italy.

00:04:00.995 --> 00:04:07.053
He has short, dark hair, exciting eyes and clothes from Sergio Taccini.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.964
His English is very bad.

00:04:10.024 --> 00:04:16.366
We go to some important buildings in Oxford, but Sonia doesn't look at the buildings.

00:04:16.426 --> 00:04:21.448
She only looks at Sylvia and Sylvia only looks at her.

00:04:21.508 --> 00:04:24.268
They don't want me there with them.

00:04:24.328 --> 00:04:28.677
I'm writing this in an internet cafe in Oxford.

00:04:28.736 --> 00:04:31.384
Are Sonia and Sylvia in love?

00:04:31.444 --> 00:04:34.737
What can I say to them on the train to London?

00:04:34.796 --> 00:04:38.059
Zero messages.

00:04:38.119 --> 00:04:44.102
Saturday, July the 23rd, 1046.

00:04:44.162 --> 00:04:46.464
It's Saturday morning.

00:04:46.524 --> 00:04:51.416
Sonia is shopping in Oxford Street with Sylvia, not with me.

00:04:51.476 --> 00:04:53.758
The laces are working.

00:04:53.818 --> 00:04:58.568
Saturday is a big day at the cinema and at the police station.

00:04:58.628 --> 00:05:06.700
There are only two people in the double-decker internet cafe, me and the owner, and 30 computers.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.132
The owner's name is Jeff.

00:05:09.191 --> 00:05:12.424
He's old, maybe 25.

00:05:12.484 --> 00:05:15.566
He has brown hair and blue eyes.

00:05:15.626 --> 00:05:18.268
Maybe he reads this blog.

00:05:18.328 --> 00:05:22.080
He asks me, do you like my cafe?

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.621
Very, very much, I say.

00:05:24.681 --> 00:05:27.573
He smiles and touches my hand.

00:05:27.633 --> 00:05:33.862
Zero messages.

00:05:33.922 --> 00:05:50.928
Chapter 2 Slow or Fast Thursday, July 28, 1541 Jeff is watching me a lot today.

00:05:50.988 --> 00:05:53.909
I look up and he smiles at me.

00:05:53.969 --> 00:05:56.320
I look back at my computer.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.762
I look up again.

00:05:57.821 --> 00:06:00.163
Again, Jeff is looking at me.

00:06:00.223 --> 00:06:01.794
Does he like me?

00:06:01.854 --> 00:06:04.984
Maybe we can be friends.

00:06:05.044 --> 00:06:08.213
I've got a message on my blog.

00:06:08.273 --> 00:06:09.944
It's from Slowboy.

00:06:10.004 --> 00:06:11.836
Thank you, Slowboy.

00:06:11.895 --> 00:06:14.678
One message.

00:06:14.738 --> 00:06:21.032
Thursday, July the 28th, 10, 18.

00:06:21.092 --> 00:06:23.434
Hello, Japanese Junko.

00:06:23.494 --> 00:06:25.496
I like reading your blog.

00:06:25.556 --> 00:06:27.917
I'm learning Japanese in Tokyo.

00:06:27.977 --> 00:06:30.158
I'm in Japan for six months.

00:06:30.218 --> 00:06:32.450
I've got one or two friends here.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:33.972
But they're new friends.

00:06:34.032 --> 00:06:36.588
Not my old friends back in London.

00:06:36.648 --> 00:06:41.338
I like Japan, but sometimes I feel lonely too.

00:06:41.398 --> 00:06:42.918
Right to me.

00:06:42.978 --> 00:06:45.520
I'm waiting for a message from you.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.892
Don't be sad, slow boy.

00:06:47.952 --> 00:06:49.764
We can be block friends.

00:06:49.823 --> 00:06:53.746
We can laugh about our problems.

00:06:53.806 --> 00:06:59.501
Tuesday, August 2nd, 1539.

00:06:59.561 --> 00:07:04.806
In the school cafe, Sonia is looking at Andreas' mobile.

00:07:04.866 --> 00:07:07.789
That's a cool mobile, she says.

00:07:07.849 --> 00:07:11.712
He answers, I'm buying Suzuki Motorbike too.

00:07:11.772 --> 00:07:13.474
I have the money.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:17.386
Sonia looks into undress his eyes and smiles.

00:07:17.446 --> 00:07:20.248
Do you like my new green t-shirt?

00:07:20.308 --> 00:07:23.342
It's from Topshop in Oxford Street.

00:07:23.402 --> 00:07:26.244
It's the color of your eyes, Sonia.

00:07:26.304 --> 00:07:28.175
Do you like my jeans?

00:07:28.235 --> 00:07:32.108
Yes, and I like the person in the jeans too.

00:07:32.168 --> 00:07:35.251
They're from Gap, she smiles.

00:07:35.311 --> 00:07:37.282
Where's Sylvia?

00:07:37.342 --> 00:07:38.352
There.

00:07:38.412 --> 00:07:40.133
He's looking at Sonia.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:42.573
But Sonia isn't looking at him.

00:07:42.633 --> 00:07:45.914
Maybe she isn't in love with him today.

00:07:45.974 --> 00:07:49.105
One message.

00:07:49.164 --> 00:07:55.375
Tuesday, August the 2nd, 10, 20.

00:07:55.435 --> 00:07:57.956
There's a girl here in Tokyo.

00:07:58.016 --> 00:08:00.516
We take the same bus every day.

00:08:00.576 --> 00:08:02.776
But she's very shy.

00:08:02.836 --> 00:08:05.824
How can I be friends with her?

00:08:05.883 --> 00:08:08.862
Be very polite, slow boy.

00:08:08.922 --> 00:08:11.144
Open the door of the bus for her.

00:08:11.203 --> 00:08:15.138
Japanese girls like polite boys.

00:08:15.198 --> 00:08:20.502
Friday, August 5, 1544.

00:08:20.561 --> 00:08:24.235
Sylvia is very quiet at school today.

00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:27.008
He's sad because of Sonia.

00:08:27.068 --> 00:08:29.930
She sits next to Andres now.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.005
Andres' family has lots of money.

00:08:33.065 --> 00:08:37.120
Andreas and Sylvia and Sonia never talk to me.

00:08:37.181 --> 00:08:38.972
But I'm not sad.

00:08:39.032 --> 00:08:41.224
I've got a blog friend.

00:08:41.284 --> 00:08:44.946
In the internet cafe, there's a hand on my back.

00:08:45.007 --> 00:08:46.077
I look up.

00:08:46.137 --> 00:08:48.178
It's Jeff, the owner.

00:08:48.238 --> 00:08:51.341
I go to a different window on the computer.

00:08:51.401 --> 00:08:53.852
He can't see my blog now.

00:08:53.912 --> 00:08:56.604
Do you want a drink, baby?

00:08:56.664 --> 00:08:57.976
Okay.

00:08:58.036 --> 00:09:00.862
Let's go to the West End on my motorbike.

00:09:00.922 --> 00:09:02.718
How can I say no?

00:09:02.778 --> 00:09:05.688
Jeff is my first friend in England.

00:09:05.748 --> 00:09:06.979
Motorbike?

00:09:07.039 --> 00:09:07.669
Now?

00:09:07.729 --> 00:09:08.580
I say.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.330
Honda, Japanese.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.391
Quiet and no problems.

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.512
Come on.

00:09:13.572 --> 00:09:16.403
We go down the street very fast.

00:09:16.463 --> 00:09:20.374
Next to the language school, Sonia and Andres are talking.

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:22.577
They see me and smile.

00:09:22.637 --> 00:09:27.802
Jeff says, friends, maybe, I don't know, I answer.

00:09:27.862 --> 00:09:29.863
I see, let's go back.

00:09:29.923 --> 00:09:31.774
We can say hello to them.

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:33.715
Can I go home now?

00:09:33.775 --> 00:09:36.396
Okay, baby, no problem.

00:09:36.456 --> 00:09:39.418
Zero messages.

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:44.622
Monday, August the 8th, 1540.

00:09:44.682 --> 00:09:47.083
Who's the boy, Junco?

00:09:47.143 --> 00:09:48.834
Sonia smiles at me.

00:09:48.894 --> 00:09:51.325
He's got a great mud bike.

00:09:51.385 --> 00:09:53.267
His name's Jeff.

00:09:53.328 --> 00:09:59.674
A honda Andres says, not bad, but I'm buying Suzuki 600.

00:09:59.734 --> 00:10:02.456
It's expensive and fast.

00:10:02.516 --> 00:10:05.368
How do you know Jeff Sonja asks?

00:10:05.428 --> 00:10:08.840
He's a friend, I answer.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:15.806
Oh, Sonja and Andres say, Sylvia is listening, but he doesn't smile.

00:10:15.866 --> 00:10:19.128
He's always sad now because of Sonia.

00:10:19.188 --> 00:10:21.069
He opens the door for me.

00:10:21.129 --> 00:10:22.740
Thank you, I say.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.740
My face is red.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.902
Sonia sits next to me.

00:10:26.962 --> 00:10:28.432
We are friends again.

00:10:28.492 --> 00:10:31.454
We talk about Jeff and Andreas.

00:10:31.514 --> 00:10:35.096
Boys and motorbikes are the same, she says.

00:10:35.156 --> 00:10:38.677
Some are exciting, some are slow.

00:10:38.737 --> 00:10:41.972
Two messages.

00:10:42.031 --> 00:10:48.498
Saturday, August the 6th, 1121.

00:10:48.558 --> 00:10:51.560
The girl on the bus is very shy.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.242
Her face is always red.

00:10:54.302 --> 00:10:56.613
She likes you, slow boy.

00:10:56.673 --> 00:10:59.785
Ask her to a cafe.

00:10:59.845 --> 00:11:05.839
Monday, August the 8th, 604.

00:11:05.899 --> 00:11:08.661
I'm coming back to England soon, Junco.

00:11:08.721 --> 00:11:10.272
Let's meet in London.

00:11:10.332 --> 00:11:16.898
Okay, great.

00:11:16.958 --> 00:11:37.127
Chapter 3 Slow Boy in London Thursday, August 11, 1547 Hi Junko Hi Jeff Come and talk to me First I want to What?

00:11:37.188 --> 00:11:39.259
What do you do on the computers?

00:11:39.319 --> 00:11:43.703
I'll write emails to my family in Japan Your family?

00:11:43.763 --> 00:11:51.480
Cool Jeff likes touching my hand He isn't shy Come to a party with me, Jinko.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.094
See you here at 830 on Saturday, okay?

00:11:55.154 --> 00:11:56.976
How can I say no?

00:11:57.036 --> 00:11:58.548
It's not polite.

00:11:58.608 --> 00:12:00.160
Okay, I say.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:01.091
Great.

00:12:01.151 --> 00:12:03.404
I love girls with glasses.

00:12:03.464 --> 00:12:06.387
Zero messages.

00:12:06.447 --> 00:12:10.769
Friday, August the 12th, 1819.

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:17.641
Silvia says, Junko, I'm going to a cafe with Petra and David from school.

00:12:17.701 --> 00:12:19.222
Can you come with us?

00:12:19.282 --> 00:12:20.573
Yes, great.

00:12:20.633 --> 00:12:21.853
Thank you.

00:12:21.914 --> 00:12:25.386
It's fun with Silvia and Petra and David.

00:12:25.446 --> 00:12:28.147
We talk about cinema and sport.

00:12:28.207 --> 00:12:31.449
I'm bad at sport and Silvia is too.

00:12:31.509 --> 00:12:34.310
But he's clever and polite.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:39.034
He asks me to the cinema on Saturday night with Petra and David.

00:12:39.094 --> 00:12:42.174
But I say, I'm going to a party.

00:12:42.234 --> 00:12:44.164
He says with who?

00:12:44.224 --> 00:12:45.825
You don't know him.

00:12:45.886 --> 00:12:47.446
Is it Jeff?

00:12:47.506 --> 00:12:50.719
How do you know about Jeff from you?

00:12:50.779 --> 00:12:51.810
Me?

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.100
Oh!

00:12:53.161 --> 00:12:56.253
I can't go to the cinema and the party.

00:12:56.313 --> 00:12:58.424
Say no to the party, Jinko.

00:12:58.484 --> 00:12:59.846
Come with us!

00:12:59.906 --> 00:13:03.968
How does Sylvia know about Jeff internet?

00:13:04.028 --> 00:13:07.331
Zero messages.

00:13:07.391 --> 00:13:12.014
Monday, August the 15th, 1538.

00:13:12.074 --> 00:13:18.128
On Saturday night, Jeff and I go to the party on his motorbike.

00:13:18.188 --> 00:13:21.620
There are 200 people in a small room.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:24.162
They are dancing and drinking.

00:13:24.222 --> 00:13:26.224
Give me your jacket, Junko.

00:13:26.284 --> 00:13:27.575
It's hot in here.

00:13:27.635 --> 00:13:29.496
Let's have a drink.

00:13:29.556 --> 00:13:31.438
Jeff is dancing.

00:13:31.498 --> 00:13:33.018
He takes my hand.

00:13:33.078 --> 00:13:34.390
I dance too.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.491
But I don't like dancing.

00:13:36.551 --> 00:13:38.302
I feel very hot.

00:13:38.363 --> 00:13:41.015
It's 1245, very late.

00:13:41.075 --> 00:13:45.558
Jeff says, give me a kiss, baby, for fun.

00:13:45.618 --> 00:13:47.370
I can't.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.102
I don't know the words for words.

00:13:51.162 --> 00:13:53.843
A kiss, baby, not words.

00:13:53.903 --> 00:13:55.464
He kisses me.

00:13:55.524 --> 00:13:57.485
I run into the next room.

00:13:57.545 --> 00:14:01.627
Then I remember, Sonia's number is on my mobile.

00:14:01.687 --> 00:14:03.408
Sonia, help me.

00:14:03.468 --> 00:14:04.718
I'm at a party.

00:14:04.778 --> 00:14:06.009
I can't get home.

00:14:06.069 --> 00:14:07.470
I haven't got a car.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:08.810
I'm in.

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.111
Where are we?

00:14:10.171 --> 00:14:11.727
I ask a girl.

00:14:11.787 --> 00:14:14.793
Belgravia Drive in Camden.

00:14:14.853 --> 00:14:18.154
We are at Belgravia Drive in Camden, Sonia.

00:14:18.214 --> 00:14:20.384
Come and find me, please.

00:14:20.444 --> 00:14:23.055
Okay, I love parties, Jinko.

00:14:23.115 --> 00:14:24.586
See you soon.

00:14:24.646 --> 00:14:29.447
Today in school, Sonia says, Great party, Jinko.

00:14:29.507 --> 00:14:30.867
I like Jeff.

00:14:30.927 --> 00:14:34.048
Andris is nice, and he's got lots of money.

00:14:34.108 --> 00:14:36.059
But Jeff is different.

00:14:36.119 --> 00:14:40.728
He's got no money now, but he's opening a second internet cafe.

00:14:40.788 --> 00:14:43.147
I've got his mobile number.

00:14:43.206 --> 00:14:45.177
Yes, yes, I say.

00:14:45.237 --> 00:14:47.048
But I feel sad.

00:14:47.108 --> 00:14:50.778
I can only go to the internet cafe at lunchtime now.

00:14:50.838 --> 00:14:53.329
Jeff isn't there at lunch.

00:14:53.389 --> 00:14:56.390
Two messages.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:15:02.731
Monday, August the 15th, 1545.

00:15:02.791 --> 00:15:04.372
I'm in London.

00:15:04.432 --> 00:15:07.072
Let's meet tomorrow at the internet cafe.

00:15:07.132 --> 00:15:09.043
At the internet cafe?

00:15:09.103 --> 00:15:11.708
I don't know.

00:15:11.768 --> 00:15:18.114
Monday, August the 15th, 1546.

00:15:18.174 --> 00:15:20.244
But lunchtime is okay.

00:15:20.304 --> 00:15:22.576
We can meet at one o'clock.

00:15:22.636 --> 00:15:24.856
Okay, at one o'clock.

00:15:24.916 --> 00:15:27.497
Jeff isn't in the cafe at lunchtime.

00:15:27.557 --> 00:15:32.248
You always remember my problems, slowboy.

00:15:32.308 --> 00:15:37.570
Tuesday, August the 16th, 1245.

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:41.626
In 15 minutes, slowboy is arriving.

00:15:41.686 --> 00:15:45.572
Jeff comes into the cafe and sits at his computer.

00:15:45.632 --> 00:15:47.292
It's lunchtime.

00:15:47.352 --> 00:15:49.194
Why is he here?

00:15:49.254 --> 00:15:50.784
I put my head down.

00:15:50.844 --> 00:15:53.226
Please don't see me, Jeff.

00:15:53.286 --> 00:15:54.566
Bing!

00:15:54.626 --> 00:15:56.498
A new message on my blog.

00:15:56.558 --> 00:15:58.528
It's from Slowboy.

00:15:58.588 --> 00:16:01.650
Four messages.

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:08.014
Tuesday, August the 16th, 1251.

00:16:08.074 --> 00:16:09.704
Hello, Junko.

00:16:09.764 --> 00:16:11.449
I'm here in the cafe.

00:16:11.509 --> 00:16:12.904
In the cafe?

00:16:12.964 --> 00:16:15.435
But there are ten boys in the cafe.

00:16:15.495 --> 00:16:18.126
Which of them is you, slow boy?

00:16:18.186 --> 00:16:20.378
Which do you think?

00:16:20.438 --> 00:16:23.029
Have you got dark hair?

00:16:23.089 --> 00:16:24.880
You know me, Junco?

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:26.501
I don't live in Tokyo.

00:16:26.561 --> 00:16:28.322
That's only a story.

00:16:28.382 --> 00:16:30.192
I live in London.

00:16:30.252 --> 00:16:31.483
A story?

00:16:31.503 --> 00:16:33.124
I know you.

00:16:33.185 --> 00:16:34.405
You mean?

00:16:34.465 --> 00:16:35.446
Yes.

00:16:35.506 --> 00:16:36.766
That's right.

00:16:36.826 --> 00:16:38.587
You like computers?

00:16:38.647 --> 00:16:40.526
I like computers.

00:16:40.586 --> 00:16:41.983
I look up.

00:16:42.043 --> 00:16:43.774
Jeff is watching me.

00:16:43.834 --> 00:16:45.104
Oh no!

00:16:45.164 --> 00:16:47.094
He smiles and gets up.

00:16:47.154 --> 00:16:49.255
Slowboy is Jeff.

00:16:49.315 --> 00:16:53.386
Then, one of the boys at the computers gets up too.

00:16:53.446 --> 00:16:54.846
It's Sylvia.

00:16:54.906 --> 00:16:56.176
He smiles.

00:16:56.236 --> 00:16:58.267
My face is red.

00:16:58.327 --> 00:17:00.978
Hello Jinko says Sylvia.

00:17:01.038 --> 00:17:03.838
Hello Jinko says Jeff.

00:17:03.898 --> 00:17:07.489
Help me internet, which is slowboy.

